          },
          {
            "id": 2770141,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "When the theatre was built, people were generally slimmer and shorter than now and the seats were very close together. We've replaced them with larger seats, with more legroom. This means fewer seats in total, but we've taken the opportunity to install seats that can easily be moved to create different acting spaces. We've also turned a few storerooms over to other purposes, like using them for meetings. We try hard to involve members of the public in the theatre.",
            "children": [
              {
